######## 

$ kagebunshin project init app
created project app with environment dev

$ kagebunshin project add-source app dev --provider aws_sm --secret acme/dev/db --profile bare
added a source to environment dev of project app; it replaces the default source, the local store's section, unless you add `--provider file` too

$ kagebunshin run -- true
kagebunshin: cannot resolve environment dev of project app: profile bare: credentials missing or expired (1 source, checked <time> UTC)
ask the human: run `aws login --profile bare` (`aws sso login` for an SSO profile)
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin next
the environment cannot be resolved
waiting on the human; tell them:
  - Please run `aws login --profile bare` in a terminal, so kagebunshin can read aws_sm (profile bare).
nothing more you can do until the human has done the above

-- the human logs in, and the daemon is not restarted

$ kagebunshin run -- sh -c 'echo the database is ${DATABASE_URL:+set}'
kagebunshin: warning: no .env.example found, so every key the environment has is passed (1 key); `kagebunshin project example` writes one from the keys the code reads, to pass only those
the database is set

-- a profile that is not there

$ kagebunshin project add-env app other
added environment other to project app

$ kagebunshin project add-source app other --provider aws_sm --secret acme/dev/db --profile nope
added a source to environment other of project app; it replaces the default source, the local store's section, unless you add `--provider file` too

$ kagebunshin --env other run -- true
kagebunshin: cannot resolve environment other of project app: aws_sm secret acme/dev/db (profile nope): AWS profile nope is not in your AWS configuration
hint: name one that is with `kagebunshin project set-source app other 1 --profile PROFILE`; `aws configure list-profiles` lists them
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin --env other next
the environment cannot be resolved
next (you): cannot resolve environment other of project app: aws_sm secret acme/dev/db (profile nope): AWS profile nope is not in your AWS configuration; name one that is with `kagebunshin project set-source app other 1 --profile PROFILE`; `aws configure list-profiles` lists them
  kagebunshin project set-source app other 1 --profile PROFILE
